# TypeScript Development Best Practices

## TypeScript Configuration

The Mobile app uses strict TypeScript configuration for maximum type safety and code quality.

### TypeScript Config

```json
// tsconfig.json
{
  "extends": "expo/tsconfig.base",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
    "exactOptionalPropertyTypes": true,
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["src/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", ".expo/types/**/*.ts", "expo-env.d.ts"]
}
```

### Path Aliases

```typescript
// Use path aliases for clean imports
import { components } from '@/components' // ✅ Correct
import { components } from '../../../components' // ❌ Avoid relative paths

// Path alias configuration
"paths": {
  "@/*": ["src/*"]
}
```

## Interface and Type Definitions

### Component Props Interfaces

```typescript
// Define comprehensive interfaces for component props
interface ComponentProps {
  title: string
  subtitle?: string
  onPress?: () => void
  disabled?: boolean
  loading?: boolean
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  children?: React.ReactNode
}

// Use descriptive interface names
interface AuthFormData {
  email: string
  password: string
  confirmPassword?: string
}

// Extend base interfaces when appropriate
interface ExtendedButtonProps extends ButtonProps {
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'outline'
  size?: 'small' | 'medium' | 'large'
}
```

### Array Type Definitions

Always use `T[]` syntax instead of `Array<T>` for better readability and ESLint compliance.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Use T[] syntax
interface User {
  id: string
  name: string
  hobbies: string[]
  permissions: Permission[]
  addresses: Address[]
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Complex array types
interface ApiResponse {
  users: User[]
  errors: ValidationError[]
  metadata: { key: string; value: unknown }[]
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Nested arrays
interface Category {
  items: Item[]
  subcategories: Category[]
}

// ❌ INCORRECT - Array<T> syntax (ESLint error)
interface BadUser {
  hobbies: Array<string>
  permissions: Array<Permission>
  addresses: Array<Address>
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Utility types with arrays
interface Gift {
  categories: Exclude<GiftCategory, 'all'>[]
  timeline: TimelineEvent[]
  tags: readonly string[]
}
```

### API Type Definitions

```typescript
// Request/Response type patterns
export interface LoginRequest {
  phone: string
  password: string
}

export interface LoginResponse extends ApiBaseResponse {
  data: {
    access_token: string
    refresh_token: string
    user: User
    expires_in: number
  }
}

// Use generic types for reusable patterns
export interface PaginatedResponse<T> {
  data: T[]
  pagination: {
    current_page: number
    per_page: number
    total: number
    last_page: number
  }
}

// Use const assertions for immutable data
export const API_ENDPOINTS = {
  AUTH: {
    LOGIN: '/auth/login',
    REGISTER: '/auth/register',
  },
  USER: {
    PROFILE: '/user/profile',
  },
} as const

type ApiEndpoint = (typeof API_ENDPOINTS)[keyof typeof API_ENDPOINTS]
```

